alder new silo: Activity: migrations/ create it in the shared database, so a database may hold rows of it: `silo org` would leave them there, unread (a migration does not move rows between databases). If no database holds rows of it yet, run this again with --empty: it also writes the migration that creates it in the silos made before, and the deploy that applies it needs --allow-data-loss (book 8, "Silos")
